## Original Content
The measures come after President Trump imposed 50% tariffs on many Canadian goods and threatened more after trade talks broke down on Friday.

## Summary
Canada has announced retaliatory tariffs on the United States in response to President Trump's imposition of 50% tariffs on Canadian goods and threats following failed trade talks. This escalation deepens the ongoing trade dispute between the two countries.

## Key Points
- Canada imposes retaliatory tariffs on the U.S.
- President Trump imposed 50% tariffs on many Canadian goods
- Trade talks broke down, leading to further threats
- The trade fight between Canada and the U.S. is intensifying


